      "result": {
        "reply_text": "For monthly-basis employees, the employer shall pay wages before the expiry of the seventh day of the succeeding month. If wages are not paid, an application for claims may be filed before the appointed authority by the employee, a registered trade union, or an Inspector-cum-Facilitator.\n\nWhat I understood: You are currently working at a private shop in Kanpur, Uttar Pradesh, and your monthly wage of 14,000 INR for October 2026 remains unpaid.\n\nThe authority may order the payment of the claim and compensation in addition to the claim, which may extend to ten times of the claim determined. An application may be filed within a period of three years from the date on which the claim arises.\n\nDocuments needed: Keep ready your appointment letter, pay slips, attendance records, or bank statements showing the non-credit of wages, and an affidavit verifying the facts.\n\nCould you please tell me the name of the shop and the exact date when the salary was due?\n\nSource: Code on Wages, 2019, section 17\nSource: Code on Wages, 2019, section 45\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
